            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gigi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "good recipe, I made a few changes, I used fresh spinach, fresh mashroom which I sauted with 1/3 chopped onion and 3 chopped garlic cloves then mixed in the rest of the ingredients. yummy",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-11T14:22:56.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Matt M"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Personally, I didn't really like this as is. So, while it was cooking, I added some chopped onions, and mozzarella and parmesian cheeses. I also sprinkled red pepper in it instead of pepper sauce. Served it over angel hair pasta. Kids loved it, even though it had spinach in it. I thought it was much better with the cheese, but still would rate it 3.5 stars with the cheese, 2 stars without the cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-14T22:10:58.677Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "OTTOS2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Although this dish was very easy to make, I found it very runny and bland. I think that the basic premise of this dish is fine, just forget about the water and add another can of cream of mushroom soup with maybe a 1/4 Cup of milk. I didn't use any water because my broccoli was partially frozen and only 1/4 or so cup of milk and still this dish was incredibly runny. I was hoping for a more thick and sauce-ier dish, not soup. Boil some instant brown rice in which helped but it was still soupy.",
            "datePublished": "2006-05-29T17:40:41.123Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made as directed. Super easy and quick. Served over Orzo.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-22T23:14:24.407Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rock_lobster"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy a la King Haiku: \"Really needed more, like sauteed onions, garlic. But very easy!\" The chicken that I used in this was ultra-flavored from a leftover marinated 'cue so I'm sure that added some oomph to an otherwise vanilla-sounding entree. But even w/o the chicken, my husband and I agreed that for the ease of putting this together, it turned out pretty tasty. Next go-around, I'll add some sauteed onion and garlic, for sure, and more than a dash of hot sauce ... and really, 1-star reviewer? 'Too many ingredients to make this easy'?",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-05T03:37:35.127Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
